SUMMARY:Author Talk: "The Cruelest Game" by Matthew Futterman
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 22 spots left\nS
 tatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/even
 ts/201348\n\nCelebrate an unforgettable summer of tennis with an inside lo
 ok at the game beyond center court. Join acclaimed sports journalist and b
 estselling author Matthew Futterman for his first Boston appearance on the
  book tour for The Cruelest Game\, an illuminating exploration of the ambi
 tion\, resilience\, and sacrifice required to succeed at the highest level
 s of professional tennis. Through remarkable access and previously untold 
 stories\, Futterman pulls back the curtain on the sport to examine the imm
 ense pressures facing established champions and the next generation of pla
 yers competing for their place among tennis’s elite.\n\nJoining Futterma
 n in conversation are former world No. 7 tennis player and Olympic silver 
 medalist\, Tim Mayotte\, and The New Yorker staff writer\, Louisa Thomas\,
  who pens the publication’s Sporting Scene column. Together\, they will 
 bring perspectives from the court and the press box to a wide-ranging conv
 ersation about professional tennis at a pivotal moment. As familiar legend
 s make way for a new generation of stars\, the evening will explore the ch
 anging landscape of the sport\, the realities behind its most celebrated v
 ictories\, and the personal price of pursuing greatness on the world stage
 . \n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complim
 entary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all
  cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/201348
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
